# App Review demo account for scripts/review_account.sh (skill heji-review-account). Sourced as bash.
# The password is never here: it lives in ~/Credentials/review-accounts.env and App Store Connect.

REVIEW_EMAIL="appreview+fitloop@hejitech.com"
# The Worker that serves POST /api/review-sign-in, and where it runs.
WORKER_DIR="projects/fitloop/services/web"
WRANGLER_ENV="production"
SITE="https://fitloop.hejitech.workers.dev"
BUNDLE_ID="com.hejitech.fitloop"

# App Store Connect › App Review Information › Notes.
REVIEW_NOTES="Sign in: on the first screen tap \"Sign in with email\" (below Continue with Google) and use the demo account above. People create accounts with Sign in with Apple or Google; email sign-in is only for accounts we hand out, such as this one.

FitLoop shows a fitness and nutrition plan that the user's own AI assistant writes (it connects over MCP from Settings > Agents). So you don't need an assistant, every sign-in with this account starts with a sample plan already published: today's workout and meals on Today, the full week on Plan. Try: open a workout and step through its sets, check off a meal, leave a note on Feedback, look at Progress.

Apple Health is optional: after sign-in FitLoop asks once to read Health data for a daily summary (Settings > Daily Apple Health summary). Declining is fine and every screen still works. Health data is never used for ads and goes to an AI agent only if the user connects one and allows it in Settings > What your agent may see. The Apple Watch app shows the workout and heart rate while a workout is open on the iPhone. The Even Realities G2 glasses (Settings > Glasses) need the glasses and aren't required. FitLoop gives no medical advice.

Account deletion: Settings > Delete my FitLoop data deletes the account and everything FitLoop keeps about it (plans, check-ins, notes, vitals, photos, devices, agent access) and signs out. The same sign-in also opens our other apps, so their data isn't touched."
